\end{figure}

%% ================================================================
%%  SECTION VII: EXPERIMENTAL RESULTS
%% ================================================================
\section{Experimental Results}
\label{sec:results}

Across the 49 controlled experiments, we analyze baseline vulnerability, countermeasure efficacy, component ablation, and post-quantum performance.

\subsection{Baseline CIL-DoS and Countermeasure Failure}
Table~\ref{tab:core_results} summarizes core results under 100K\,pps attack, separating measured host hardware from projected embedded relay profiles.
Under pure FIFO scheduling evaluated on the calibrated Substation Embedded Relay Profile ($\overline{S} = 573\,\mu$s, $\mu = 1{,}745$\,fps), RSA-2048 verification saturates immediately, yielding a mean latency of 2,318\,ms ($K \cdot \overline{S} = 4{,}096 \times 566\,\mu\text{s}$) and \textbf{100\% deadline violations}. On the High-Speed Host Platform ($\overline{S} = 33.7\,\mu$s, $\mu = 29{,}689$\,fps), a single worker also saturates under 100K\,pps flood ($\rho_1 = 3.37 > 1$), exceeding the 3\,ms deadline at 138.0\,ms saturated queue wait ($K \cdot \overline{S} = 4{,}096 \times 33.7\,\mu\text{s} = 138{,}035\,\mu$s).

\textbf{Na\"ive Countermeasure 1 (Buffer Bloat):} Increasing queue size from 4,096 to 16,384 packets increases latency from 2,318\,ms to 9,264\,ms ($4\times$ increase) while maintaining 100\% deadline failure (Fig.~\ref{fig:buffer_workers}a). Buffering exacerbates CIL-DoS.

\textbf{Na\"ive Countermeasure 2 (Parallel Workers):} Deploying 4 verification workers on the relay profile increases aggregate throughput from 1,745 to 6,980\,fps. However, because $\lambda_{\text{atk}} = 100{,}000\,\text{pps} \gg 6{,}980$, queue utilization remains $\rho_4 = 14.3 \gg 1$. Latency drops to 579\,ms, but \textbf{deadline violations remain at 100\%} (Fig.~\ref{fig:buffer_workers}b). (On the host platform, 4 workers scale throughput to $118{,}756$\,fps, shifting queue saturation to 500K\,pps where $\rho_4 = 4.21 \gg 1$ and 100\% deadline failure recurs).

