\subsection{PQAC Defense and Latency Reconcilement}
As shown in Table~\ref{tab:core_results} and Figs.~\ref{fig:latency_vs_rate}--\ref{fig:deadline_miss}, PQAC delivers substantial latency reductions without cross-platform distortion. To provide complete transparency across evaluation configurations, we define and report three operational regimes:
\begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{SCD Pre-Provisioned Profile (Standard Substation Engineering):} Standard IEC~61850 engineering specifies pre-configuring authorized IED parameters (MAC addresses, \texttt{appID}, \texttt{gocbRef}) via Substation Configuration Description (SCD) files. With $\mathcal{M}$ provisioned at startup, legitimate protection frames bypass learning and enter Class~$H$ immediately. In this production profile, PQAC achieves an end-to-end delivered mean latency of \textbf{65.4\,$\mu$s}, a P99 of \textbf{164.8\,$\mu$s}, and \textbf{0.00\% deadline violations} ($2,110\times$ latency reduction over host FIFO baseline).
    \item \textbf{Dynamic Learning Steady State (657.8\,$\mu$s):} In retrofit deployments without pre-configured SCD allowlists, MACs are learned dynamically. Once the sliding-window tracker accumulates history ($t > 0.5$\,s), legitimate frames are isolated from flood traffic, achieving \textbf{0.00\% deadline miss} with P99 of \textbf{944.1\,$\mu$s}.
    \item \textbf{Dynamic Learning Session-Wide Mean (1,489.6\,$\mu$s):} When evaluated across an entire 60-second benchmark starting cold simultaneously with an aggressive 100K\,pps attack, the initial $\sim$0.5\,s learning transient produces an overall session miss rate of \textbf{2.45\%} (P99 = 4,820\,$\mu$s). Once converged, the system transitions to zero-miss steady state.
\end{enumerate}

