%% ================================================================
%%  SECTION VIII: LAYERED DEFENSE ARCHITECTURE
%% ================================================================
\section{Layered Defense Architecture}
\label{sec:defense}

To guard against MAC spoofing at extreme flood rates ($>$500K\,pps), we specify a defense-in-depth architecture:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*,noitemsep,topsep=1pt]
    \item \textbf{Layer 1 (NIC Driver eBPF/XDP):} Wire-speed packet filtering executing in $<0.5\,\mu$s at the network driver level. Drops invalid EtherTypes, enforces per-MAC token-bucket rate limits, and suppresses spoofed sources prior to kernel socket memory allocation.
    \item \textbf{Layer 2 (Application PQAC):} High-precision rate anomaly detection, burst preservation, and priority queue dispatching.
    \item \textbf{Layer 3 (Cryptographic Engine):} Asymmetric/PQC verification on prioritised frames with constant-time execution.
\end{itemize}

Table~\ref{tab:defense_comparison} compares this layered scheme against conventional substation defenses, showing that only eBPF/XDP + PQAC provides line-rate filtering without latency penalties.

